In addition, I join Sebastian's request regarding how can n be defined for hierarchical models.

For example, if this is my model:

Yij ~ N(µj,σj)       //observation i of group j, both mean and variance are unknown
µj ~ N(meanYj,SE_meanYj)  //meanYj is the sample mean of group j, and SE_meanYj is its standard error
σj ~ HalfCauchy(γ) //γ would either be an empirical value or a hyperparameter distributed γ ~ U(0,∞)

Thanks a lot,
rubi

