As Bob said, all of the code is publicly viewable in our repository (the implementation is in src/stan/mcmc/hmc/nuts/base_nuts.hpp).  The refactor uses a new, but equivalent, termination criterion as described in http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.1920, but otherwise is just aimed at making the algorithm easier to follow.  The best debugging tool I had was the old implementation - I knew I had it right when, given the same initial position and momentum and random numbers, the two algorithms built the exact same trees.

